  min_success_chance: "Cost per success and expected total cost never pick a model whose chance of solving work at the request's level is below this (0–1). A model exactly at the level has the chance a 5 has on the reference work (the anchor: 70% on FrontierSWE for coding), so 0.6 lets in models a little below the level and no further. If no model reaches it, the threshold decides. Default 0.6.",
  human_cost_usd: "Expected total cost: what a failed attempt at the top of the scale (a level-5 agent task) costs the person who asked, in dollars, on top of the tokens: noticing it, saying so, waiting for the redo. Minutes of their time times their hourly rate: the default $1 is one minute at $60 an hour. A request puts a share of it at stake: a third for each level below 5, less again under 8,000 tokens, all of it after a correction. Higher sends more work to stronger models; 0 counts only tokens. Teams can set their own (Controls). Default 1.",
