  user: "The ClickHouse user. It needs to create tables in the database, and to insert, select and delete there. Default `default`.",
  password_env: "Environment variable on the gateways and the worker that holds the password. Default MERITORDER_CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD. The password itself is never stored here.",
  password_file: "A file holding the password, such as a mounted Kubernetes Secret. Read again when it changes, so a rotated password works without a restart. If it's missing or empty, the variable is used.",
  reads: "large: reports over more than 7 days and tag breakdowns read ClickHouse. all: every summary, export, GPU what-if and bill comparison does too. none: ClickHouse only gets the copy, for your own tools or while a backfill runs. Budgets and the request list always read Postgres. Default large.",
